(* A primitive that fails where its entry was recorded: `=` and
   `printString` on a user subclass of `String`, whose instances carry no
   string, fall through the failure block's `super` send -- `printString`
   to `Object`'s, and `=` to `Value`'s, since §3.1.1 puts `String` under
   `Value`. `Value`'s leaf declines a `Text` too (its `=` is `String`'s,
   not `Value`'s), so the Newspeak walk answers, comparing the classes and
   then zero slots. The recorded `true` is unchanged only because every
   line here compares an object with *itself*: two distinct `Text`
   instances would now answer `true` as well, where `Object`'s identity `=`
   answered `false` (`goldens/library/value/a_value_has_no_identity.ns` records
   that). `show:` answers two transcript streams and fails on the platform
   object, which shares their class, so the third send at the same site --
   the same dispatch id -- ends in `doesNotUnderstand:`
   (`docs/design/dispatch.md`, "A primitive can fail").

   The module is declared a value (`Object <: Value`, §3.1.1) because it
   declares a value class, `Text` below `String`, and a value class's
   enclosing object must be a value; the transcript is therefore read where
   it is used, never held in a slot. *)
class CacheFailingPrimitive = Object <: Value () (
    class Text = String new () (
    )
    public main: platform args: args = (
        | text transcript |
        transcript:: platform transcript.
        text:: Text new.
        {'abc'. text. 'abc'. text} do: [:each |
            transcript show: (each = each) printString; show: ' '; show: each printString; newLine].
        {platform transcript. platform. platform transcript} do: [:each |
            transcript show: (each = each) printString; newLine].
        {'abc'. {1. 2}} do: [:each | transcript show: each size printString; newLine].
        {platform transcript. platform transcript. platform} do: [:each | each show: 'shown'. each newLine].
    )
) : ()
